[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Install with Vortex or MO2; manual installs are not supported.[/b] The installer opens with a check of your setup and refuses to run without CBBE.
[list=1]
[*]Install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url] 1.2.0 and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url], then Anatomy.
[*]Get [b]AnatomyBuilder 1.2.0[/b] from [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy/releases/tag/v1.2.0]GitHub[/url], extract it into a folder of its own and run [font=Courier New]AnatomyBuilder.exe[/font] once (MO2: add it to MO2's executables, like BodySlide).
[*]In BodySlide, build "Anatomy Body" with your preset. Men: build "Anatomy Male Body" (or "... Uncut") instead of BodyTalk4.
[*]Optional: AnatomyRebuild, from the same page, after every BodySlide build, for the hip fix on your outfits.
[/list]
[b]Upgrading from 1.1.1:[/b] install Engine 1.2.0 then Anatomy 1.2.0 over the old ones, run AnatomyBuilder 1.2.0 again and rebuild in BodySlide. Saves carry on.

[b]Pre-built bodies (optional files):[/b] two ready-built bodies on the Files tab, [b]Zeroed[/b] and [b]Ivy[/b], for players who'd rather not run the builder. They were built with Anatomy 1.1.1: [b]no vaginal lining[/b]; run the builder for it. Their genitals are textured against the vanilla skin, and they carry no .tri (CBBE's team asks that players build those in BodySlide). Still needed: CBBE with its BodySlide files, BodySlide, the Anatomy Engine and Anatomy. Used with the permission of Ousnius and the CBBE team.

[quote]
[b]Needs:[/b] the Anatomy Engine 1.2.0, F4SE, [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url], CBBE 2.7.2 with its BodySlide files, BodySlide. Fallout 4 1.10.163 or the Anniversary Edition.
[b]Optional:[/b] AAF (scenes), Rapport (moans, faces, glances), LooksMenu (nipples, glans colour), MCM (settings), BodyTalk 4 with its BodySlide files (M-M), 3BBB with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/39006]Skeletal Adjustments for CBBE[/url], any physics preset (Anatomy brings its own).

[b]Nothing of another mod is overwritten.[/b] Anatomy's physics lines sit in their own folder and are read after yours; the builder writes only new files, each in one step, and stops with a clear message rather than guess.
[b]Anatomy tells you in game if F4SE or the Engine is missing[/b] (since 1.2.1): a message box naming the fix, only when something is wrong.
[/quote]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]Incompatibilities[/color][/b][/size]

Known conflicts, from real reports and the code. Found another one? Tell us in the Bugs tab.
[list]
[*][b]Animated Fannies (LoversLab 4302)[/b]: both build the same body file (FemaleBody.nif), so the last build wins. Anatomy already includes its vulva and anus, rebuilt; build only "Anatomy Body".[/*]
[*][b]Other women's bodies (BodyTalk women, Fusion Girl, or any mod replacing the body file other than CBBE 2.7.2 or 3BBB)[/b]: the builder refuses them, because the genitals fit those bodies only.[/*]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/105699]OCBP LPCE[/url][/b]: its own physics DLL, which replaces the Anatomy Engine, so the genital physics, mouth and aim go dead. Use one or the other.[/*]
[*][b]BodyTalk3 men[/b]: untested; the redder-glans overlay is drawn for BodyTalk4, so on BodyTalk3 switch "Glans colour" off in MCM.[/*]
[*][b]BC7 skins (many 4K skin mods, e.g. Unfair Skin)[/b]: they work, but the builder can't write BC7, so it stores the genitals' colour texture uncompressed: about 5 MB at 4K with AnatomyBuilder 1.0.11 (about 85 MB with older builders), slightly heavier than a DXT skin. Re-run the latest builder and rebuild "Anatomy Body".[/*]
[*][b]Men's skeletons other than [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/36702]ZeX - ZaZ Extended Skeleton[/url][/b]: the penis aim needs ZeX's linked penis bones (Penis_00 to Penis_05 in one chain). With any other men's skeleton the aim switches itself off (the log says so) and the penis keeps the animation's own pose. Use ZeX 6.0 for the men.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb547]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Something looks wrong. What do I send?[/b]
[spoiler]The Bugs tab, with Anatomy_Health.txt (My Games\Fallout4\F4SE): the engine writes it about 10 s after every load and names the engine, the preset, the body and every simulated actor.[/spoiler]

[b]What are the two tools?[/b]
[spoiler]The Anatomy Builder and Anatomy Rebuild are Python tools packed to run without installing Python. They are not in the Nexus download. Their source is in [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-anatomy]the public repository[/url] ([font=Courier New]tools/builder.py[/font], [font=Courier New]tools/rebuild.py[/font]).[/spoiler]

[b]Does it work with my other mods?[/b]
[spoiler]AAF and UAP, LooksMenu, Rapport, Silhouette (nipples stay flat under heavy armour it marks), Overture and Ivy (arousal sources), CBBE HeadRear Absolute Fix, any OCBPC physics config, BodyTalk4 men, and Anatomy Tailor's refits.[/spoiler]

[b]Where are the settings?[/b]
[spoiler]MCM, page "Anatomy": the arousal nipples and their strength, rise and fade speed, each arousal source, and the glans colour. The sticky posts list every feature and setting.[/spoiler]

